Configures CoreCLR for Linux from any host, without the parts of its build that are not libcoreclr or libclrgc.

* eng/native/tryrun.cmake supplies the results of the configure's checks that run a program, which a cross build
  cannot run. It takes the results for macOS whenever the machine configuring has /System/Library/CoreServices,
  whatever the target, so on a macOS host it would describe a Linux build by macOS's answers (HAS_POSIX_SEMAPHORES
  among them). The target here is always Linux.
* src/coreclr/CMakeLists.txt adds the single-file host and the System.Native family of shims. Configuring them would
  need trees of src/native/libs that the flake's sparse checkout leaves out, and headers, such as krb5's, that the
  sysroot does not hold.

One line of context, so that the patch applies to every pinned runtime: the lines around each hunk differ between
them.

--- a/eng/native/tryrun.cmake
+++ b/eng/native/tryrun.cmake
@@ -41,4 +41,2 @@
     set(CLR_CMAKE_TARGET_OS sunos)
-  elseif(EXISTS /System/Library/CoreServices)
-    set(DARWIN 1)
   elseif(EXISTS ${CROSS_ROOTFS}/etc/tizen-release)
--- a/src/coreclr/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/coreclr/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -71,4 +71,2 @@
   set(CLR_SINGLE_FILE_HOST_ONLY 1)
-  add_subdirectory(${CLR_SRC_NATIVE_DIR}/corehost/apphost/static Corehost.Static)
-  add_dependencies(runtime singlefilehost)
 endif()
@@ -86,3 +84,2 @@
   set(STATIC_LIBS_ONLY 1)
-  add_subdirectory(${CLR_SRC_NATIVE_DIR}/libs libs-native)
 endif()
